From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH perf 001] panvk/csf: emit the cache clean once per subqueue per batch

kbase_subqueue_emit_job() emitted a 0x233 CS flush (clean+invalidate
L2/LSC, invalidate other caches) in front of every job. In a batch of N
jobs on the same subqueue, jobs 2..N re-clean caches that cannot hold
new CPU writes: pan_kmod_flush_bo_map_syncs() already published every CPU
write of the batch before the ioctl, and ring entries on one subqueue are
executed in order, so the first job's clean covers all of them.

- Add a flush_caches argument and emit the flush only when it is set.
- Track a flushed mask per submit: the first job of each subqueue in the
  batch flushes, later jobs on the same subqueue do not.
- A subqueue that never appears in the batch is unaffected.
- The queue-init stream keeps its unconditional flush.

Purpose: drop redundant CS cache-flush instructions from multi-job submits.
Tested GPU: build only, not yet run on device.
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21.
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f).
Dependencies: none (perf series is appended last).
Validation test: TBD, on-device render smoke test.

Generated-by: LLM

